  "query_preview": "..\nSynoptic Setup: A cold front will continue to push south on \nThursday, bringing any lingering showers across southern portions \nof the CWA to an eventual end. Otherwise look for mostly cloudy \nskies and cool temperatures across the area.\n\nZonal northwest upper flow late this week into the weekend will\nlead to mainly dry weather and near seasonable temperatures.\nHowever,a weak shortwave tracking southeast is showing up in some\nof the ensemble members, so cannot rule out a remote shower Friday\nnight or Saturday. Confidence is not great enough to reflect this\nin the pops.\n\nUpper ridging looks to build in from the west on Monday.\nIncreasing heights and large scale subsidence will maintain a dry\nweather presence for NE Montana as well as warming temperatures.\nHighs in the afternoon may reach into the 70s and 80s.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nPersistent showers continue across the southern zones but will\ngradually diminish and shift south into Thursday. The next weak\nshortwave looks to arrive on Friday night into Saturday but\nconfidence is low on any showers at this time. Confidence is\ngrowing as ensembles continue to show wider support for upper\nriding early next week and warmer temperatures. \n\nOverall NBM handled the forecast cycle well, though nudged \nThursday morning lows down in a few valley locations and into the \nnortheast where clouds will occur later. Given the complication of\ncloudiness, confidence on Thursday morning lows is somewhat lower\nthan average. Pops were also adjusted to come in line with \ncurrent reflectivity and observations and near term expectations.",
